    <!-- DOC PROCESS -->
    <div class="guide" id="guide-doc-process">
      <div class="guide-header">
        <div class="guide-eyebrow">Product documentation</div>
        <div class="guide-title">How to: documentation process</div>
        <div class="guide-desc">End-to-end process for getting capability and module docs published on docs.kaluza.com</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tabs">
        <button class="tab-btn active" onclick="switchTab(this,'dp')">Step-by-step</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(this,'dp')">Jira setup</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(this,'dp')">Review & approval</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(this,'dp')">Rules & tips</button>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel active" id="dp-0">
        <p class="section-title">The full process</p>
        <p class="section-sub">From initiative to published doc — what you do, in order.</p>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">1</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Create your ADIS epic in Jira <span class="badge badge-warn">Do this first</span></div><div class="step-desc">Create an epic in the <strong>CALAU project</strong> to track all documentation tasks. Name it clearly — e.g. "Product Documentation — [Module Name] ✍️" — and list the capability docs to be created in the description. Add a pencil emoji so it's easy to spot.</div><div class="tip"><i class="ti ti-clock"></i> Do this as soon as you know a new doc will be needed.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">2</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Link to the KDSM board</div><div class="step-desc">Link your ADIS epic to the relevant Life Support parent ticket on the KDSM board using the <strong>"relates to"</strong> link type. If there's no suitable parent, create a new one. Not sure which to use? Ask in <strong>#ask-documentation</strong>.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">3</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Set the documentation due date</div><div class="step-desc">The due date is <strong>3 weeks before the feature release date</strong>. This deadline is non-negotiable.</div><div class="tip"><i class="ti ti-alert-circle"></i> Your draft must be in review at least 2 weeks before deadline.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">4</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Draft your doc using Claude or the Gemini Gem</div><div class="step-desc">All drafts must be in <strong>Google Docs</strong>. Make sure the tech writer has <strong>edit access</strong> before submitting, or the doc will be rejected.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">5</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Create a KDSM child ticket <span class="badge badge-info">Per doc</span></div><div class="step-desc">Add a sub-task to the KDSM board for each capability doc. Include the document title (matching the <strong>Kaluza Product Capability Matrix</strong> naming) and the relevant release label. Do not create your own label.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">6</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Submit for review <span class="badge badge-warn">≥1 week before deadline</span></div><div class="step-desc">Add the Google Doc link to the KDSM ticket, assign to the tech writer, move to <strong>In Review</strong>, and post in <strong>#ask-documentation</strong>.</div><div class="channel-box"><div class="channel-label">#ask-documentation</div><div class="channel-text">Hey @[doc team lead], can you please review the [capability doc] for [initiative]: [KDSM-XXX]</div></div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">7</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Review cycle</div><div class="step-desc">Tech writer reviews, suggests edits, reassigns back to you. Once happy, leave a comment confirming approval and reassign back to publish.</div><div class="channel-box"><div class="channel-label">Approval comment</div><div class="channel-text">Happy with the edits — approved for publishing</div></div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">8</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Mark ADIS epic as Done <span class="badge badge-success">Published!</span></div><div class="step-desc">Once published, set the ADIS epic to <strong>Done</strong> and include a link to the portal page in the ticket description.</div></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel" id="dp-1">
        <p class="section-title">Jira ticket setup</p>
        <p class="section-sub">Three tickets involved — here's how they connect.</p>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num accent">A</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">ADIS epic (CALAU project)</div><div class="step-desc">Main tracking ticket. Name: "Product Documentation — [Module] ✍️". Due date = release date minus 3 weeks. Link to KDSM via <strong>relates to</strong>.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num accent">B</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">KDSM topic ticket</div><div class="step-desc">The parent ticket on the KDSM board for your product area. Link your ADIS epic here via "relates to".</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num accent">C</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">KDSM child ticket (one per doc)</div><div class="step-desc">Sub-task of the topic ticket. Name must match the Kaluza Product Capability Matrix. Assign release label. One ticket per Google Doc — do not combine.</div><div class="warn-inline"><i class="ti ti-alert-triangle"></i> Never point multiple tickets at a single doc.</div></div></div>
        <div class="divider"></div>
        <p class="section-heading">ADIS epic statuses</p>
        <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px;margin-bottom:1rem">
          <div class="status-badge"><div class="dot" style="background:#9E9E98"></div>Not started</div>
          <div class="status-badge"><div class="dot" style="background:#1E3FAA"></div>In progress</div>
          <div class="status-badge"><div class="dot" style="background:#1A6B40"></div>Done</div>
          <div class="status-badge"><div class="dot" style="background:#8A2020"></div>Not required</div>
        </div>
        <div class="callout callout-warn"><strong>Not required</strong> If documentation isn't needed, set this status and add a mandatory comment explaining why (e.g. "Internal-only feature" or "Minor bug fix with no client impact").</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel" id="dp-2">
        <p class="section-title">Review & approval</p>
        <p class="section-sub">Who reviews what, and in what order.</p>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-user-check" style="color:var(--success-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Subject matter expert (you)</div><div class="rule-desc">You are responsible for accuracy and completeness. The tech writer checks language and format — not your product facts.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-pencil" style="color:var(--info-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Tech writer review (mandatory)</div><div class="rule-desc">Checks clarity, consistency, formatting, and style. Will suggest edits and reassign back to you.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-users" style="color:var(--text-muted)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Peer review (optional)</div><div class="rule-desc">A colleague can review for accuracy before you submit to the tech writer.</div></div></div>
        <div class="callout callout-warn" style="margin-top:1rem"><strong>Don't share with clients before internal review</strong> Sharing draft docs externally before internal review creates bad first impressions and risks roadmap commitments. Internal review always comes first.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel" id="dp-3">
        <p class="section-title">Rules & tips</p>
        <p class="section-sub">Things that commonly trip people up.</p>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-file-type-doc" style="color:var(--info-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Google Docs only</div><div class="rule-desc">All drafts must be in Google Docs with edit access granted to the tech writer. Any other format is rejected.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-tag" style="color:var(--warn-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Never create your own release label</div><div class="rule-desc">Ask in #ask-documentation if the right label doesn't exist. Duplicates cause problems for the tech writer's workload management.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-world" style="color:var(--success-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Write global-first</div><div class="rule-desc">Docs are reused across clients. No KEG (use Streaming API), no KAPI (use Synchronous API), no client-specific language unless marked appropriately.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-sitemap" style="color:var(--text-primary)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Use the Kaluza Product Capability Matrix for naming</div><div class="rule-desc">Doc titles must match the KPM. If your module isn't in the KPM, speak to your Head of Department first.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-user" style="color:var(--success-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">AU tech writer is Amy Halford</div><div class="rule-desc">Share docs with amy.halford@kaluza.com (edit access) before assigning the KDSM ticket.</div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- DOC CLAUDE -->
    <div class="guide" id="guide-doc-claude">
      <div class="guide-header">
        <div class="guide-eyebrow">Product documentation</div>
        <div class="guide-title">How to: create docs using Claude</div>
        <div class="guide-desc">Using the /product-documentation skill to draft capability docs ready for tech writer review</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tabs">
        <button class="tab-btn active" onclick="switchTab(this,'dc')">Before you start</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(this,'dc')">What to ask Claude</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(this,'dc')">BE vs FE docs</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(this,'dc')">After the doc is created</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(this,'dc')">Tips</button>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel active" id="dc-0">
        <p class="section-title">Before you start</p>
        <p class="section-sub">Have these ready before asking Claude to write anything.</p>
        <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden">
          <div class="checklist-item"><i class="ti ti-circle-1"></i><div><div class="check-label">Module name and description</div><div class="check-desc">A short explanation of what the module does and the business domain it covers — e.g. "Life Support is the module that manages customers who rely on life-sustaining medical equipment"</div></div></div>
          <div class="checklist-item"><i class="ti ti-circle-2"></i><div><div class="check-label">Initiative ticket(s)</div><div class="check-desc">The parent KAL-XXXX initiative and any BE or FE delivery tickets</div></div></div>
          <div class="checklist-item"><i class="ti ti-circle-3"></i><div><div class="check-label">Initiative spec Confluence URL</div><div class="check-desc">If one exists — Claude will fetch and read it as part of drafting</div></div></div>
          <div class="checklist-item"><i class="ti ti-circle-4"></i><div><div class="check-label">Figma links</div><div class="check-desc">For any FE work — Claude will use these to describe the agent-facing UI</div></div></div>
          <div class="checklist-item"><i class="ti ti-circle-5"></i><div><div class="check-label">BE doc, FE doc, or both?</div><div class="check-desc">Decide before you start — see the BE vs FE docs tab for what each covers</div></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel" id="dc-1">
        <p class="section-title">What to ask Claude</p>
        <p class="section-sub">Use this prompt as your starting point — fill in the bracketed sections.</p>
        <div class="prompt-box">Use /product-documentation to create a capability doc for [feature name].

Module: [module name and short description]

Initiative: [KAL-XXXX — link]
BE delivery tickets: [CALAU-XXX or similar — link]
FE delivery tickets: [KAL-XXXX — link]
Initiative spec: [Confluence page URL]
Figma: [Figma file URL if available]

Please also search for any other related initiatives or specs under [parent initiative ticket].

I need: [BE doc / FE doc / both]</div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num"><i class="ti ti-search" style="font-size:12px"></i></div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Fetch all tickets and spec pages</div><div class="step-desc">Reads your Jira tickets, Confluence spec, and Figma links. Also searches for related initiatives you may have missed.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num"><i class="ti ti-pencil" style="font-size:12px"></i></div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Draft the capability doc(s)</div><div class="step-desc">Uses the Kaluza template and style guide to produce a structured draft — BE doc, FE doc, or both.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num"><i class="ti ti-file-text" style="font-size:12px"></i></div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Create Google Docs ready for review</div><div class="step-desc">Outputs the draft(s) as Google Docs. Apply formatting and add screenshots before submitting to the tech writer.</div><div class="tip"><i class="ti ti-info-circle"></i> Google Docs from Claude won't have rich formatting — apply heading styles manually.</div></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel" id="dc-2">
        <p class="section-title">BE vs FE docs</p>
        <p class="section-sub">Two different docs for two different audiences.</p>
        <div class="doc-type-card"><div class="doc-type-label" style="color:var(--info-text)"><i class="ti ti-server" style="font-size:12px;margin-right:3px"></i>BE capability doc</div><div class="doc-type-title">What the platform does — retailer and business perspective</div><div class="doc-type-items">— Functional capability, business rules, and compliance behaviour<br>— What the system enforces, triggers, and records<br>— Outputs, reporting, and data availability<br>— Non-technical throughout — no architecture or code references</div></div>
        <div class="doc-type-card"><div class="doc-type-label" style="color:var(--success-text)"><i class="ti ti-layout" style="font-size:12px;margin-right:3px"></i>FE capability doc</div><div class="doc-type-title">What agents see and do — the interface experience</div><div class="doc-type-items">— What agents see and do at each step of the journey<br>— Structured workflows, guided forms, and validation behaviour<br>— Role-based controls and what is blocked or restricted<br>— Screen-by-screen UI reference with screenshot placeholders<br>— Still non-technical — no component names or code references</div></div>
        <div style="padding:12px 14px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);background:var(--surface-raised)"><p style="font-size:13px;font-weight:500;color:var(--text-primary);margin-bottom:4px">When both are needed</p><p style="font-size:12px;color:var(--text-secondary)">Claude creates two separate Google Docs:</p><div class="mono-box">[Feature] – Capability Doc DRAFT (BE)<br>[Feature] – Capability Doc DRAFT (FE)</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel" id="dc-3">
        <p class="section-title">After the doc is created</p>
        <p class="section-sub">Seven steps from Claude output to published on the docs site.</p>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">1</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Create your ADIS epic <span class="badge badge-info">Ask Claude</span></div><div class="step-desc">Ask Claude: "Can you create an ADIS epic for [feature name] under [KAL-XXXX]?"</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">2</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Prepare your Google Doc</div><div class="step-desc">Review the draft, make edits, add screenshots from Figma. Share with amy.halford@kaluza.com (edit access) before submitting.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">3</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Create KDSM sub-tasks <span class="badge badge-info">Ask Claude</span></div><div class="step-desc">Ask Claude: "Can you create KDSM sub-tasks for [feature name]?"</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">4</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Check your ADIS epic links</div><div class="step-desc">Verify "relates to" links between KDSM sub-tasks and your ADIS epic are in place before submitting.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">5</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Submit for review <span class="badge badge-warn">≥1 week before deadline</span></div><div class="step-desc">Add Google Doc link, assign to tech writer, move to In Review, post in #ask-documentation.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">6</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Review cycle</div><div class="step-desc">Tech writer reviews, reassigns to you. Approve edits and leave a comment on the ticket.</div><div class="channel-box"><div class="channel-label">Approval comment</div><div class="channel-text">Happy with the edits — approved for publishing</div></div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">7</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Close your ADIS epic <span class="badge badge-success">Done!</span></div><div class="step-desc">Once all KDSM sub-tasks are published and marked Done, mark your ADIS epic as Done.</div></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel" id="dc-4">
        <p class="section-title">Tips</p><p class="section-sub">Common mistakes to avoid.</p>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-text-size" style="color:var(--info-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Apply formatting manually in Google Docs</div><div class="rule-desc">Apply Heading 1 to the doc title, Heading 2 to each section, and use Google Docs list formatting for bullet points.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-photo" style="color:var(--text-muted)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Fill in screenshot placeholders from Figma</div><div class="rule-desc">Claude always includes screenshot placeholders — export from Figma and paste into the doc before submitting.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-tag" style="color:var(--warn-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Never create your own release label</div><div class="rule-desc">Ask in #ask-documentation if the right one doesn't exist.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-layout-sidebar" style="color:var(--text-muted)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Check the docs site structure first</div><div class="rule-desc">If the module doesn't yet have a section on the Kaluza docs site, raise with the tech writer before submitting — a new section may need to be created first.</div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- RN PROCESS -->
    <div class="guide" id="guide-rn-process">
      <div class="guide-header">
        <div class="guide-eyebrow">Release notes</div>
        <div class="guide-title">How to: release note process</div>
        <div class="guide-desc">End-to-end process for getting a release note drafted, reviewed, and published on docs.kaluza.com</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tabs">
        <button class="tab-btn active" onclick="switchTab(this,'rp')">Overview</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(this,'rp')">Step-by-step</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(this,'rp')">Roles</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(this,'rp')">Review & approval</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(this,'rp')">Tips</button>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel active" id="rp-0">
        <p class="section-title">What is a release note?</p>
        <p class="section-sub">A release note describes new functionality available to clients as part of a release. A single release note may cover several initiatives.</p>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-refresh" style="color:var(--info-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Published for every client release</div><div class="rule-desc">Kaluza publishes a release note for every client release. Notes are organised into a quarterly page on the docs site per client, with the most recent at the top.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-users" style="color:var(--text-muted)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Master note + sub-notes</div><div class="rule-desc">Each release has one master release note made up of sub-notes per product area. Individual PMs submit their own sub-note. The tech writer compiles them and publishes on release day.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-calendar" style="color:var(--warn-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Submit at least 2 weeks before the release date</div><div class="rule-desc">Your draft must be in the KDSM ticket, moved to In Review, and assigned to the tech writer at least 2 weeks before the release date.</div></div></div>
        <div class="divider"></div>
        <p class="section-heading">Templates</p>
        <div class="grid-2">
          <div class="field-card"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:var(--info-text);margin-bottom:4px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em">New docs site</div><div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--text-secondary)">Use for SEA, AGL, Engie and all new clients on docs.kaluza.com</div></div>
          <div class="field-card"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:var(--text-muted);margin-bottom:4px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em">Legacy dev portal</div><div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--text-secondary)">Use for OVO only — the legacy portal is still live for OVO UK</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel" id="rp-1">
        <p class="section-title">Step-by-step process</p>
        <p class="section-sub">Follow these steps as soon as you know a release note is needed.</p>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">1</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Create a KDSM ticket <span class="badge badge-warn">Do this first</span></div><div class="step-desc">As soon as you know you need a release note, create a ticket on the KDSM board in Drafting. Name it after the content. Add it as a sub-task of the relevant master release note task.</div><div class="tip"><i class="ti ti-clock"></i> Don't wait until the draft is done — create the ticket immediately.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">2</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Add the release label</div><div class="step-desc">Add the relevant release label from the right-hand column. Do not create your own — ask in <strong>#ask-documentation</strong> if the right one doesn't exist.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">3</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Draft using Claude or the template</div><div class="step-desc">All drafts must be in <strong>Google Docs</strong>. Make sure the tech writer has edit access.</div><div class="tip"><i class="ti ti-info-circle"></i> See "How to: write a release note" for what to include in each section.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">4</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Submit for review <span class="badge badge-warn">≥2 weeks before release</span></div><div class="step-desc">Add Google Doc link, assign to tech writer, move to In Review.</div><div class="channel-box"><div class="channel-label">#ask-documentation</div><div class="channel-text">Hey @[name], can you please review the [release note] for [release name]: [KDSM-XXX]</div></div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">5</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Review cycle</div><div class="step-desc">Tech writer reviews, reassigns back to you. Approve edits and leave a comment on the ticket.</div><div class="channel-box"><div class="channel-label">Approval comment</div><div class="channel-text">Happy with the edits — approved for publishing</div></div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">6</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Tech writer publishes <span class="badge badge-success">Done!</span></div><div class="step-desc">Tech writer adds your sub-note to the master release note and publishes on release day.</div></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel" id="rp-2">
        <p class="section-title">Roles</p><p class="section-sub">Who does what.</p>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-user" style="color:var(--info-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Primary author (PM or release manager)</div><div class="rule-desc">Owns the release note for their product area. Selects template, writes the intro, coordinates contributors, and submits on time.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-pencil" style="color:var(--text-muted)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Tech writer (Amy Halford for AU)</div><div class="rule-desc">Reviews for clarity, style, and consistency. Compiles sub-notes into the master. Publishes on release day. Contact: amy.halford@kaluza.com</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-building" style="color:var(--text-muted)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">AU client contacts</div><div class="rule-desc">AGL: Amy Halford (Mel Santo) — SEA: Hayden Phyo (Deanne). Help coordinate client-specific content and manage publication timing expectations.</div></div></div>
        <div class="divider"></div>
        <p class="section-heading">Release note skeleton</p>
        <div class="mono-box">[CLIENT NAME] [MONTH] Release [RELEASE NO]<br>Target release date: [date]<br>Summary: [2–3 sentence overview]<br><br>[Product area 1] — @[author]<br>[Product area 2] — @[author]</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel" id="rp-3">
        <p class="section-title">Review & approval</p><p class="section-sub">Internal review always comes before the client sees anything.</p>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-user-check" style="color:var(--success-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">You are responsible for accuracy</div><div class="rule-desc">The tech writer checks language and style — not product facts. Ensure content is accurate and complete before submitting.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-pencil" style="color:var(--info-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Tech writer review is mandatory</div><div class="rule-desc">All content goes through tech writer review. Respond via ticket comments, not Slack.</div></div></div>
        <div class="callout callout-warn" style="margin:1rem 0"><strong>Don't share with clients before internal review</strong> Draft release notes shared externally can lead to clients treating roadmap content as commitments.</div>
        <p class="section-heading">Review order</p>
        <div class="review-flow">
          <div class="review-step">Peer review <span style="font-weight:400;color:var(--text-muted)">(optional)</span></div>
          <span class="review-arrow">→</span>
          <div class="review-step mandatory">Tech writer review (mandatory)</div>
          <span class="review-arrow">→</span>
          <div class="review-step">Publish</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel" id="rp-4">
        <p class="section-title">Tips</p>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-clock" style="color:var(--warn-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Create the KDSM ticket early</div><div class="rule-desc">The tech writer plans workload based on what's in the KDSM board. Last-minute tickets cause bottlenecks.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-tag" style="color:var(--warn-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Never create your own release label</div><div class="rule-desc">Ask in #ask-documentation. Duplicates make the tech writer's job harder and slow down publishing.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-file-type-doc" style="color:var(--info-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Google Docs only, with edit access</div><div class="rule-desc">Share amy.halford@kaluza.com with edit access before moving the ticket to In Review.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-message-circle" style="color:var(--text-muted)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Use ticket comments, not Slack, for feedback</div><div class="rule-desc">Keeps a clear record and avoids things getting lost.</div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- RN WRITE -->
    <div class="guide" id="guide-rn-write">
      <div class="guide-header">
        <div class="guide-eyebrow">Release notes</div>
        <div class="guide-title">How to: write a release note</div>
        <div class="guide-desc">What goes in each section, how to write it, and what to avoid</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tabs">
        <button class="tab-btn active" onclick="switchTab(this,'rw')">Before you write</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(this,'rw')">Sections guide</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(this,'rw')">Ask Claude</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(this,'rw')">Style rules</button>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel active" id="rw-0">
        <p class="section-title">Before you write</p><p class="section-sub">Have these ready before opening the template.</p>
        <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden">
          <div class="checklist-item"><i class="ti ti-circle-1"></i><div><div class="check-label">The module or feature name</div><div class="check-desc">This becomes the heading — informative and precise, no exclamation marks</div></div></div>
          <div class="checklist-item"><i class="ti ti-circle-2"></i><div><div class="check-label">The KAL initiative ticket(s)</div><div class="check-desc">Claude will fetch these to understand what changed and why</div></div></div>
          <div class="checklist-item"><i class="ti ti-circle-3"></i><div><div class="check-label">Client / region</div><div class="check-desc">e.g. Global, AGL, SEA, Engie, OVO UK</div></div></div>
          <div class="checklist-item"><i class="ti ti-circle-4"></i><div><div class="check-label">Target release date and release number</div><div class="check-desc">e.g. 30th May 2026, R3.4</div></div></div>
          <div class="checklist-item"><i class="ti ti-circle-5"></i><div><div class="check-label">Initiative spec or Confluence URL</div><div class="check-desc">If one exists — helps Claude understand the full context</div></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel" id="rw-1">
        <p class="section-title">Sections guide</p><p class="section-sub">What to write in each section, and what to avoid.</p>
        <div class="section-card"><div class="section-name"><i class="ti ti-h-1" style="font-size:15px;color:var(--text-muted)"></i> Heading</div><div class="section-guidance">The module or feature name. Keep it informative and precise. If not globally applicable, make it region-specific.</div><div class="do-box">✓ Life Support — Notification Management for AU retailers</div><div class="avoid-box">✗ Exciting new Life Support updates! 🎉</div></div>
        <div class="section-card"><div class="section-name"><i class="ti ti-align-left" style="font-size:15px;color:var(--text-muted)"></i> Intro paragraph</div><div class="section-guidance">2–3 sentences maximum. State what changed and why it matters. Focus on the present and future state only — do not describe how things used to work.</div><div class="do-box">✓ Kaluza now automatically sends life support notifications to distributors when a customer's status changes, removing the need for manual intervention.</div><div class="avoid-box">✗ Previously, agents had to manually send notifications. We have now fixed this by...</div></div>
        <div class="section-card"><div class="section-name"><i class="ti ti-list" style="font-size:15px;color:var(--text-muted)"></i> Features / highlights</div><div class="section-guidance">What has changed. Use a single sentence if only one highlight. Bullets if multiple. Bold feature name, then plain language description. End last bullet with a full stop.</div><div class="mono-box">- <strong>Automatic distributor notifications:</strong> The platform sends notifications as soon as a life support flag is added or removed.<br>- <strong>Audit trail:</strong> All notifications are logged against the customer record.</div></div>
        <div class="section-card"><div class="section-name"><i class="ti ti-bulb" style="font-size:15px;color:var(--text-muted)"></i> Improvements</div><div class="section-guidance">2–4 sentences on why this change happened and what value it creates. No technical jargon.</div><div class="do-box">✓ Automating notifications removes a manual, error-prone step and reduces the risk of missed notifications for vulnerable customers.</div><div class="avoid-box">✗ We refactored the service to use an async event-driven architecture with a Kafka topic...</div></div>
        <div class="section-card"><div class="section-name"><i class="ti ti-book" style="font-size:15px;color:var(--text-muted)"></i> Reference info</div><div class="section-guidance">Practical how-to guidance, API endpoints, market interactions. Use real endpoint and parameter names from tickets. Do not link to internal Google Docs or Confluence.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel" id="rw-2">
        <p class="section-title">Ask Claude to draft it</p><p class="section-sub">Use this prompt with the /product-documentation skill.</p>
        <div class="prompt-box">Use /product-documentation to write a release note for [feature/module name].

Module: [module name and short description]

Initiative: [KAL-XXXX — link]
Initiative spec: [Confluence URL if available]

Client / region: [e.g. AGL / AU / Global]
Release number: [e.g. R3.4]
Target release date: [e.g. 30th May 2026]

I need a release note for the new docs site template.</div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num"><i class="ti ti-search" style="font-size:12px"></i></div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Fetch tickets and specs</div><div class="step-desc">Reads your Jira initiative and Confluence spec to understand the full scope of what changed.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num"><i class="ti ti-pencil" style="font-size:12px"></i></div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Draft the release note</div><div class="step-desc">Produces a complete draft — heading, intro, features, improvements, reference info — using the Kaluza style guide.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num"><i class="ti ti-file-text" style="font-size:12px"></i></div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Create a Google Doc</div><div class="step-desc">Outputs the draft as a Google Doc ready for your review. Apply heading styles manually before submitting.</div><div class="tip"><i class="ti ti-info-circle"></i> Review for accuracy — you are the subject matter expert.</div></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel" id="rw-3">
        <p class="section-title">Style rules</p><p class="section-sub">The Kaluza style guide applied to release notes.</p>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-clock" style="color:var(--info-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Present tense, active voice</div><div class="rule-desc">"The platform sends notifications automatically" — not "Notifications will be sent" or "are sent by the platform".</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-eye-off" style="color:var(--danger-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Never describe the old behaviour</div><div class="rule-desc">Do not write "Previously..." or "We have fixed..." — describe only what the product does now.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-calendar-off" style="color:var(--danger-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">No roadmap dates or timescales</div><div class="rule-desc">Clients may treat them as commitments. Only describe what is live or being released in this note.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-world" style="color:var(--success-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">No internal Kaluza terms</div><div class="rule-desc">KEG → Streaming API. KAPI → Synchronous API. No links to internal Google Docs or Confluence. No "global/local" as used internally.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-flag" style="color:var(--info-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">British English throughout</div><div class="rule-desc">Subsidised, flavour, organisation, recognise. Kaluza is "Kaluza" (not "we"). Address the reader as "you".</div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- EX PROCESS -->
    <div class="guide" id="guide-ex-process">
      <div class="guide-header">
        <div class="guide-eyebrow">Exceptions</div>
        <div class="guide-title">How to: get an exception created</div>
        <div class="guide-desc">Your end-to-end responsibilities — from identifying a new exception through to ongoing quality after go-live</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tabs">
        <button class="tab-btn active" onclick="switchTab(this,'ep')">Overview</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(this,'ep')">Step-by-step</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(this,'ep')">Statuses</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(this,'ep')">Business readiness</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(this,'ep')">Ongoing quality</button>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel active" id="ep-0">
        <p class="section-title">What you own</p><p class="section-sub">Getting an exception created isn't just a template exercise — you own the full lifecycle from detection to resolution to prevention.</p>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-file-description" style="color:var(--info-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">You write the template — engineering builds the config</div><div class="rule-desc">The engineering team handles all code configuration once your exception template is approved. Nothing can be built in code without approval.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-users" style="color:var(--text-muted)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Reviewed by the Exception Management team</div><div class="rule-desc">Lucie Hajkova and Florencia Galeano review all templates for quality and consistency. Submit in <strong>#ask-exception-management</strong>.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-refresh" style="color:var(--warn-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Your responsibility doesn't end at go-live</div><div class="rule-desc">You're accountable for exception quality ongoing — accuracy, intuitiveness, and ease of resolution.</div></div></div>
        <div class="divider"></div>
        <p class="section-heading">The three quality principles</p>
        <div class="grid-3">
          <div class="quality-pill"><i class="ti ti-target" style="color:var(--success-text)"></i><div class="qp-name">Accurate</div><div class="qp-desc">Fires when it should, doesn't when it shouldn't</div></div>
          <div class="quality-pill"><i class="ti ti-bulb" style="color:var(--info-text)"></i><div class="qp-name">Intuitive</div><div class="qp-desc">Agent understands what happened and why</div></div>
          <div class="quality-pill"><i class="ti ti-check" style="color:var(--warn-text)"></i><div class="qp-name">Easy to resolve</div><div class="qp-desc">Clear path with no ambiguity</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel" id="ep-1">
        <p class="section-title">Step-by-step process</p><p class="section-sub">Each step gates the next — nothing goes to code before the template is approved.</p>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">1</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Read the ownership cheat sheet</div><div class="step-desc">Read the Exception Ownership Cheat Sheet before starting — it explains your full responsibilities across the lifecycle.</div><div class="tip"><i class="ti ti-external-link"></i> kaluza.atlassian.net/wiki/x/nwJlJQ</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">2</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Copy and fill the Exception Template <span class="badge badge-warn">Your main job</span></div><div class="step-desc">Copy the Exception Template — never edit the original. Fill in all fields. Create your copy in the Exception catalogue. Set status to <strong>Planned</strong>.</div><div class="warn-inline"><i class="ti ti-alert-triangle"></i> Replace all grey italic placeholder text before submitting.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">3</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Submit for quality review <span class="badge badge-info">Update status to In Review</span></div><div class="step-desc">Share in <strong>#ask-exception-management</strong> and ask Lucie Hajkova or Florencia Galeano to review.</div><div class="channel-box"><div class="channel-label">#ask-exception-management</div><div class="channel-text">Hey @[Lucie / Florencia], can you please review the exception template for [exception name]: [link]</div></div><div class="callout callout-danger" style="margin-top:10px"><strong>Hard blocker</strong> Nothing can be configured in code until this is approved. Do not ask engineering to start until you have written approval.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">4</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Engineering configure in code <span class="badge badge-success">Approved</span></div><div class="step-desc">Once approved, engineering sets up the configuration. Update status to <strong>Testing</strong> once deployed to test environment.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">5</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Complete business readiness <span class="badge badge-warn">Before go-live</span></div><div class="step-desc">All business readiness steps must be complete before the exception is triggered in production. See the Business Readiness tab.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">6</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Go live and track quality <span class="badge badge-success">Live</span></div><div class="step-desc">Update status to <strong>Live</strong>. Keep tracking quality outcomes in the template and iterate based on feedback.</div></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel" id="ep-2">
        <p class="section-title">Exception statuses</p><p class="section-sub">Set the correct status at each stage.</p>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num" style="font-size:11px;font-family:'DM Mono',monospace">PL</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Planned</div><div class="step-desc">You've identified a need and have a validation rule in mind, but nothing is built yet. You're in discovery or early delivery.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num" style="font-size:11px;font-family:'DM Mono',monospace">PM</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Planned Migration</div><div class="step-desc">You're already raising this exception in OEA production via the old case management API and need to migrate it to FSA exception management after Q2 2026.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num accent">IR</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">In Review</div><div class="step-desc">You've completed the template and submitted it to the Exception Management team. Nothing goes to code until this moves to Approved.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num" style="background:var(--success-bg);color:var(--success-text);border-color:var(--success-border)">AP</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Approved</div><div class="step-desc">The Exception Management team has confirmed it fits the cohesive retailer experience. Engineering can now configure in code.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num" style="background:var(--warn-bg);color:var(--warn-text);border-color:var(--warn-border)">NV</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">New version to deploy</div><div class="step-desc">You've made changes to the Confluence template that require a new version in code. Still needs to be reflected in the codebase.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num" style="font-size:11px;font-family:'DM Mono',monospace">TE</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Testing</div><div class="step-desc">Deployed to test environment or shadow running. No retailer impact yet. Finalise business readiness with the retailer at this stage.</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num" style="background:var(--success-bg);color:var(--success-text);border-color:var(--success-border)">LV</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Live</div><div class="step-desc">Deployed to production, visible to retailer agents. You are now accountable for ongoing quality.</div></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel" id="ep-3">
        <p class="section-title">Business readiness before go-live</p><p class="section-sub">All of these must be in place before the exception is triggered in production.</p>
        <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:1rem">
          <div class="checklist-item"><i class="ti ti-school" style="color:var(--info-text)"></i><div><div class="check-label">Agents and retailer teams are trained</div><div class="check-desc">Agents know how to identify, action, and resolve the exception. It's clear how exceptions fit into work distribution.</div></div></div>
          <div class="checklist-item"><i class="ti ti-article" style="color:var(--info-text)"></i><div><div class="check-label">Knowledge articles are updated</div><div class="check-desc">Retailers have up-to-date handling guidance available when the exception appears.</div></div></div>
          <div class="checklist-item"><i class="ti ti-building" style="color:var(--info-text)"></i><div><div class="check-label">The client is informed and aligned</div><div class="check-desc">The client knows the exception is coming and is aligned on the rollout plan.</div></div></div>
          <div class="checklist-item"><i class="ti ti-list-check" style="color:var(--info-text)"></i><div><div class="check-label">Work distribution is confirmed</div><div class="check-desc">It's clear how actionable exceptions will be distributed to agents, particularly platform exceptions that don't appear on retailer work lists.</div></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="callout callout-warn"><strong>Platform and non-operations exceptions need special attention</strong> These don't appear on retailer work lists. You must document who in Kaluza resolves them and how — any gap blocks automated actions like billing.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel" id="ep-4">
        <p class="section-title">Ongoing quality after go-live</p><p class="section-sub">Going live is the start, not the end.</p>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-chart-bar" style="color:var(--info-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Track performance metrics in the template</div><div class="rule-desc">Keep updated: % of unbilled attributed to this exception, average volume per month, average time to resolve, resolution rate. Use the Tableau reporting links in the template.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-message-report" style="color:var(--warn-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Log quality problems in the tracking table</div><div class="rule-desc">If the exception isn't accurate, intuitive, or easy to resolve, log it in the quality performance table. Tag the quality dimension, add evidence, and set a resolution state.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-users" style="color:var(--text-muted)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Gather feedback from agents and ops managers</div><div class="rule-desc">Actively check with retailer stakeholders whether the exception is working as intended. An exception is only deemed high quality when those resolving it say so.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-refresh" style="color:var(--success-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Keep the template in sync with code</div><div class="rule-desc">If you update the template, set status to <strong>New version to deploy</strong> so engineering know a code change is needed.</div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- EX TEMPLATE -->
    <div class="guide" id="guide-ex-template">
      <div class="guide-header">
        <div class="guide-eyebrow">Exceptions</div>
        <div class="guide-title">How to: fill in the exception template</div>
        <div class="guide-desc">What goes in each field, and how to write a path to resolution that passes review first time</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tabs">
        <button class="tab-btn active" onclick="switchTab(this,'et')">Before you start</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(this,'et')">Header fields</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(this,'et')">Path to resolution</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(this,'et')">Quality tracking</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(this,'et')">Tips</button>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel active" id="et-0">
        <p class="section-title">Before you start</p><p class="section-sub">Three things to do before opening the template.</p>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">1</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Copy the template — never edit the original</div><div class="step-desc">Make a copy from the Exception Template page and save it in the Exception catalogue alongside all others.</div><div class="tip"><i class="ti ti-external-link"></i> kaluza.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/EM/pages/630128676</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">2</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Read the Exception Ownership Cheat Sheet</div><div class="step-desc">Explains the three quality dimensions — accurate, intuitive, easy to resolve — before you start writing.</div><div class="tip"><i class="ti ti-external-link"></i> kaluza.atlassian.net/wiki/x/nwJlJQ</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="step-num">3</div><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label">Set the exception status to Planned</div><div class="step-desc">Set the status field to <strong>Planned</strong> to indicate you're working on it. Update as it moves through review, testing, and go-live.</div></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel" id="et-1">
        <p class="section-title">Header fields</p><p class="section-sub">Fill in the header table at the top of your template copy.</p>
        <div class="field-card"><div class="field-name">Exception type <span class="req-badge req-yes">Required</span></div><div class="field-guidance">A short, clear name for what the exception represents — what agents and ops teams will see.</div><div class="field-example">e.g. Unbilled — Missing meter read</div></div>
        <div class="field-card"><div class="field-name">Reference code <span class="req-badge req-yes">Required</span></div><div class="field-guidance">A unique code from configuration. Format: two-letter product area prefix + two-digit number.</div><div class="field-example">e.g. AA01, BL03, LS02</div></div>
        <div class="field-card"><div class="field-name">Exception retailer(s) <span class="req-badge req-yes">Required</span></div><div class="field-guidance">List all retailers that will have this exception available when live. If global, say so.</div><div class="field-example">e.g. AGL, SEA — or — All retailers</div></div>
        <div class="field-card"><div class="field-name">Responsible team <span class="req-badge req-yes">Required</span></div><div class="field-guidance">Link to your team's Confluence space. Makes it clear who owns the exception for escalation and quality accountability.</div></div>
        <div class="field-card"><div class="field-name">Business impact <span class="req-badge req-yes">Required</span></div><div class="field-guidance">What happens when this exception is open and unresolved? Does it block billing? Create compliance risk?</div><div class="do-box">✓ When open, this exception blocks the billing cycle for the affected account — the customer will not receive a bill until resolved.</div><div class="avoid-box">✗ This exception means something went wrong with the meter data.</div></div>
        <div class="field-card"><div class="field-name">Kaluza initiative spec <span class="req-badge req-note">If available</span></div><div class="field-guidance">Link to the Confluence initiative spec. Helps the review team and future owners understand the full context.</div></div>
        <div class="field-card"><div class="field-name">Performance metrics <span class="req-badge req-note">Fill after go-live</span></div><div class="field-guidance">% of unbilled, average volume, average time to resolve, resolution rate. Leave blank initially — plug to Tableau once live.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel" id="et-2">
        <p class="section-title">Scenarios and path to resolution</p><p class="section-sub">The most important section — write it for agents, not for yourself.</p>
        <div class="field-card"><div class="field-name">Describe the scenario</div><div class="field-guidance">What caused the exception to fire? What went wrong and why does it matter? Must be self-contained — don't make agents click elsewhere to understand what happened.</div><div class="do-box">✓ This exception fires when the billing engine cannot generate a bill because no meter read has been received for the account in the last 90 days.</div></div>
        <div class="field-card"><div class="field-name">Path to resolution — Retailer operations</div><div class="field-guidance">If agents or CCaaS will resolve this, list the exact steps including which tools they need. Test whether these steps match what agents actually do.</div><div class="mono-box">1. Open the customer account in KAE<br>2. Navigate to Meter Reads → Request manual read<br>3. Submit a meter read request to the distributor<br>4. Once received, the billing engine will retry automatically<br>5. Mark the exception as resolved</div></div>
        <div class="field-card"><div class="field-name">Path to resolution — Platform exceptions</div><div class="field-guidance">If Kaluza resolves this, document exactly who and how. These don't appear on retailer work lists — any gap blocks automated actions.</div><div class="avoid-box">✗ Do not leave platform exceptions without a documented owner — open ones block billing and won't be picked up automatically.</div></div>
        <div class="field-card"><div class="field-name">Path to resolution — External dependency</div><div class="field-guidance">If the exception self-heals when market data arrives, document the expected timeline, any monitoring steps, and when to escalate if it doesn't self-heal.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel" id="et-3">
        <p class="section-title">Quality tracking table</p><p class="section-sub">Log quality problems here after go-live — or even during testing.</p>
        <div class="field-card"><div class="field-name">Quality problem</div><div class="field-guidance">Describe what doesn't work as intended — inaccurate firing, confusing language, missing resolution steps, or anything that makes the exception harder to handle.</div></div>
        <div class="field-card"><div class="field-name">Quality impact dimension</div><div class="field-guidance">Tag which dimension is affected.</div><div style="display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:8px"><div style="padding:3px 10px;border-radius:20px;font-size:11px;font-weight:500;background:var(--danger-bg);color:var(--danger-text);border:1px solid var(--danger-border)">Accuracy</div><div style="padding:3px 10px;border-radius:20px;font-size:11px;font-weight:500;background:var(--info-bg);color:var(--info-text);border:1px solid var(--info-border)">Intuitiveness</div><div style="padding:3px 10px;border-radius:20px;font-size:11px;font-weight:500;background:var(--warn-bg);color:var(--warn-text);border:1px solid var(--warn-border)">Ease to resolve</div></div></div>
        <div class="field-card"><div class="field-name">Evidence</div><div class="field-guidance">How frequent or severe is the problem? Include data from Tableau, agent feedback, or escalation counts. Evidence drives prioritisation.</div></div>
        <div class="field-card"><div class="field-name">State</div><div class="field-guidance">Move through: Backlog → Solution agreed → On roadmap → Delivery → Resolved.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="tab-panel" id="et-4">
        <p class="section-title">Tips</p><p class="section-sub">What gets templates bounced back in review.</p>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-italic" style="color:var(--danger-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Replace all grey italic placeholder text</div><div class="rule-desc">Templates with instructional placeholder text still in place are sent straight back. Every instruction must be replaced with real content.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-user" style="color:var(--info-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Write the path to resolution for agents, not for yourself</div><div class="rule-desc">Imagine an agent seeing this for the first time with no prior knowledge. Every step must be explicit — which tool, which screen, which action. "Check the account" is not a step.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-alert-triangle" style="color:var(--warn-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Don't leave platform exceptions without an owner</div><div class="rule-desc">Platform exceptions don't appear on retailer work lists. No named resolver = exceptions sitting open indefinitely.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-refresh" style="color:var(--success-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">Keep the template in sync with code at all times</div><div class="rule-desc">If you update the template post-approval, set status to <strong>New version to deploy</strong>. The template is the source of truth.</div></div></div>
        <div class="rule-card"><i class="ti ti-copy" style="color:var(--danger-text)"></i><div><div class="rule-title">One template per exception type</div><div class="rule-desc">Do not combine multiple exception types into a single template page.</div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </main>
</div>

<script>
function showGuide(id) {
  document.querySelectorAll('.guide').forEach(g => g.classList.remove('active'));
  document.querySelectorAll('.sidebar-item').forEach(b => b.classList.remove('active'));
  document.getElementById('guide-' + id).classList.add('active');
  document.querySelectorAll('.sidebar-item').forEach(b => {
    if (b.getAttribute('onclick').includes("'" + id + "'")) b.classList.add('active');
  });
  window.scrollTo(0, 0);
  if (id === 'calendar') buildCalendar();
}

function switchTab(btn, prefix) {
  const guide = btn.closest('.guide');
  const tabs = btn.parentElement.querySelectorAll('.tab-btn');
  const idx = Array.from(tabs).indexOf(btn);
  tabs.forEach(t => t.classList.remove('active'));
  btn.classList.add('active');
  guide.querySelectorAll('.tab-panel').forEach((p, i) => {
    p.classList.toggle('active', i === idx);
  });
}

function buildCalendar() {
  const today = new Date(); today.setHours(0,0,0,0);

  const releases = [
    { name: 'AGL R3.4', client: 'AGL', sitDate: '2026-05-28' },
    { name: 'SEA SR4',  client: 'SEA', sitDate: '2026-05-28' },
    { name: 'AGL R3.5', client: 'AGL', sitDate: '2026-06-30' },
    { name: 'SEA SR5',  client: 'SEA', sitDate: '2026-06-30' },
    { name: 'SEA SR6',  client: 'SEA', sitDate: '2026-08-31' },
    { name: 'SEA SR7',  client: 'SEA', sitDate: '2026-09-30' },
    { name: 'SEA SR8',  client: 'SEA', sitDate: '2026-10-29' },
    { name: 'SEA SR9',  client: 'SEA', sitDate: '2026-11-30' },
    { name: 'AGL R3 Go-live', client: 'AGL', sitDate: '2026-12-01' },
    { name: 'SEA SR10', client: 'SEA', sitDate: '2026-12-01' },
  ];

  function addDays(dateStr, days) {
    const d = new Date(dateStr);
    d.setDate(d.getDate() + days);
    return d;
  }

  function fmt(d) {
    return d.toLocaleDateString('en-AU', { day: 'numeric', month: 'short', year: 'numeric' });
  }

  function daysUntil(d) {
    return Math.round((d - today) / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));
  }

  function status(d) {
    const diff = daysUntil(d);
    if (diff < 0) return { label: 'Deadline passed', color: '#8A2020', bg: '#FFF0F0', border: 'rgba(138,32,32,0.2)' };
    if (diff <= 7) return { label: 'This week', color: '#8A5C00', bg: '#FFF8EC', border: 'rgba(138,92,0,0.2)' };
    if (diff <= 21) return { label: 'Coming up', color: '#1E3FAA', bg: '#EEF4FF', border: 'rgba(30,63,170,0.2)' };
    return { label: 'On track', color: '#1A6B40', bg: '#EDFAF3', border: 'rgba(26,107,64,0.2)' };
  }

  function clientBadge(client) {
    if (client === 'AGL') return 'background:#E8F0FE;color:#1E3FAA;border:1px solid rgba(30,63,170,0.2)';
    return 'background:#EDF7F0;color:#1A6B40;border:1px solid rgba(26,107,64,0.2)';
  }

  const container = document.getElementById('cal-cards');
  container.innerHTML = '';

  releases.forEach(r => {
    const sit = new Date(r.sitDate);
    const docDeadline = addDays(r.sitDate, -21);
    const rnDeadline = addDays(r.sitDate, -14);
    const s = status(docDeadline);
    const daysToDoc = daysUntil(docDeadline);
    const daysToRN = daysUntil(rnDeadline);

    const card = document.createElement('div');
    card.style.cssText = 'background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:16px;margin-bottom:10px';

    const overdue = daysToDoc < 0;
    const leftBorderColor = overdue ? '#8A2020' : daysToDoc <= 7 ? '#8A5C00' : daysToDoc <= 21 ? '#1E3FAA' : '#1A6B40';
    card.style.borderLeft = `3px solid ${leftBorderColor}`;

    card.innerHTML = `
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;margin-bottom:10px">
        <div>
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin-bottom:4px">
            <span style="font-size:14px;font-weight:600;color:var(--text-primary)">${r.name}</span>
            <span style="font-size:11px;font-weight:500;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:20px;${clientBadge(r.client)}">${r.client}</span>
          </div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--text-secondary)">SIT date: <strong style="color:var(--text-primary)">${fmt(sit)}</strong></div>
        </div>
        <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:500;padding:3px 10px;border-radius:20px;background:${s.bg};color:${s.color};border:1px solid ${s.border};white-space:nowrap">${s.label}</div>
      </div>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:8px">
        <div style="padding:10px 12px;border-radius:var(--radius-sm);background:var(--surface-raised);border:1px solid var(--border)">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--text-muted);margin-bottom:4px">Product doc deadline</div>
          <div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:500;color:var(--text-primary)">${fmt(docDeadline)}</div>
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:${daysToDoc < 0 ? '#8A2020' : daysToDoc <= 7 ? '#8A5C00' : 'var(--text-muted)'};margin-top:2px">${daysToDoc < 0 ? 'Deadline passed' : daysToDoc === 0 ? 'Due today' : daysToDoc + ' days away'}</div>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:10px 12px;border-radius:var(--radius-sm);background:var(--surface-raised);border:1px solid var(--border)">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--text-muted);margin-bottom:4px">Release note deadline</div>
          <div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:500;color:var(--text-primary)">${fmt(rnDeadline)}</div>
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:${daysToRN < 0 ? '#8A2020' : daysToRN <= 7 ? '#8A5C00' : 'var(--text-muted)'};margin-top:2px">${daysToRN < 0 ? 'Deadline passed' : daysToRN === 0 ? 'Due today' : daysToRN + ' days away'}</div>
        </div>
      </div>`;

    container.appendChild(card);
  });
}
</script>
</body>
</html>
